An additional zero-owner private-output inventory now requires review before
browser modules gain logging, debugging, error reporting, dialogs, printing,
notifications, native sharing, or clipboard binary-write authority. Fourteen
synthetic probes and six restored inactive TypeScript/JavaScript mutations
exercise the guard. This is a static review of declared browser sources, not
an OS clipboard/notification inspection, leak-free-browser proof, or fix for
the known opener argv exposure.

The File System Access picker inventory did not cover ordinary browser file
inputs, FileReader, or drag-and-drop FileList intake. A red-first source probe
added `<input type="file">` to the static HTML, `FileReader` in authored
