The HTML resource guard now also requires review for file-type inputs and
browser directory/capture input attributes. A separate source review covers
FileReader, drag-and-drop file handles and lists, binary blobs, and object URL
creation across all ten authored/emitted modules. Four static-markup and
thirteen browser-code probes plus six individually restored source mutations
verify rejection. This is a conservative lexical source review, not proof of
browser file-picker permission, drag-and-drop dataflow, or complete local-file
intake confinement; P8 acceptance remains open.

The reviewed browser modules also admitted a new inbound `message` event
listener even though outbound popup, channel, and `postMessage` APIs were
